<article class="env-corollary" id="E744">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E744">Corollary <span data-tag="E744">7.3.2.9</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a $0$-localic $\infty $-topos, associated to the locale $\calU $, and let $U \in \calU $. Then $\calX /U$ is a $0$-localic $\infty $-topos associated to the locale $\{  V \in \calU : U \subseteq V \} $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The $\infty $-topos $\calX /U$ is a topological localization of a $0$-localic $\infty $-topos, and therefore also $0$-localic (Proposition <a href="/tag/B345" data-tag="B345">6.4.5.9</a>). The identification of the underlying locale follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/E8BE" data-tag="E8BE">7.3.2.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>